  "notes": "A relatively formal word used in technical, scientific, and news contexts. In everyday speech, くっつく or つく is more natural. The particle に marks the surface something sticks to, while が marks the substance that adheres.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {汚|よご}れが{付着|ふちゃく}する (dirt sticks to)\n- {細菌|さいきん}が{付着|ふちゃく}する (bacteria adhere to)\n- {付着|ふちゃく}{物|ぶつ} (adhered substance, deposit)\n- {付着|ふちゃく}{力|りょく} (adhesive force)",
